<li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-11"><a href="#References"><span class="tocnumber">8</span> <span class="toctext">References</span></a></li>
</ul>
</div>

<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Background">Background</span></h2>
<ul><li>Typically divided into penetrating and abdominal trauma</li>
<li>Gun shot wounds that penetrate the peritoneum virtually all have intra-abdominal injury requiring surgery
<ul><li>Small bowel most commonly injured</li></ul></li></ul>
<h3><span id="Classes_of_hemorrhagic_shock.5B1.5D"></span><span class="mw-headline" id="Classes_of_hemorrhagic_shock[1]">Classes of <a href="/wiki/Hemorrhagic_shock" title="Hemorrhagic shock">hemorrhagic shock</a><sup id="cite_ref-1" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-1"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup></span></h3>
<table class="wikitable">
<tbody><tr>
<th>Class
</th>
<th>I
</th>
